<description>&lt;p&gt;President De la Espriella has ordered the temporary militarization of Cúcuta and deployed troops to the Venezuelan border city amid rising violence, while also expanding the military presence in other border areas. The government has charged nine former FARC commanders with war crimes and is conducting an anti-narcotics operation that has prompted questions over civilian killings. Cuts to the country’s human rights court under De la Espriella threaten the institution that oversees such abuses. The UN Security Council has extended the Colombian verification mission mandate through October 2027. The conflict recorded 225 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMipgFBVV95cUxPc1ZSZlJhZnhXbWtIVDhwaTZWeGVLQlo5LVhGZ3kzcnVicUQ5dXVEOFNCWDlZcHR6M2YyV2NVN0pCTGphYy1sTlpLbXp0dXB5ekk0c0p2Z1A5N3AxVTB6dGVxajVKLTJHcGFiVW82a21HenJTdkQzcndRV21uaXc5R1ZTWk9JVlUwU3B2OVlyYVNSakZ3d0JVcWRPY3pzcG94UlJXZGd3?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New York Times&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivwFBVV95cUxOZ0xmamlRUG9zWXZseVZPSFJIQkd2dncwMzFiclREUEt2Nlh6aDh5Sm5PeWpqamNVRUtIN3FxU3lNSHI2akpzUUQyb25BSGxmRF9jaUdPWlBGbGppc2JULUJMaHFxaC1wWGROV3dsQ3MtZFdaUjFnUmpSYnRJMFV6NGM1Rk1VZjlBWmNMX1dZMUxkVmc0YndQOWR6ejlFVUFQMFlwTFdqYVY5T1JBbkpHTnd1cHVJNlBfSUd1TGU3TQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;MambaOnline&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMilwFBVV95cUxNbVlDQy1yakFGN2N2WW1BVUZVYy1tRWRwNzBPNXdYWlNiQWtINldHVlFUUlp1NlBRaklNaFVEVE5IN3M3N285aVRjUXk3WDdOYXV5TVdQNUg5S3lrOF9OeENVOWVpZGlRcVg1dlh3VnNCTkIxRmRjTXFCQWhkQTZHTG8zdm1COU1HY1hBV0pKbGpIdjFPaTNN?oc=5&quot;&gt;UrduPoint&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;InsightTrendsWorld&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://